<title>ROMANIA: STRONG GALES CLOSE ROMANIA BLACK SEA PORTS.</title>
<headline>STRONG GALES CLOSE ROMANIA BLACK SEA PORTS.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strong gales hit Romania's Black Sea coast and closed traffic in the maritime ports of Constanta and Mangalia, the Transport Ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>Constanta port administration chief Jorj Unciuleanu said traffic in the two ports had been closed since Sunday night when winds of 7.0 degrees on the Beaufort scale hit the area.</p>
<p>Romania was swept by heavy rainfalls and snow as well as low temperatures over the past week.</p>
<p>No disruptions of rail, road or air traffic were reported.</p>
